			<div class="content" id="post-content-4824267">
									

<p><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6846344&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605937808" alt="JamaisJ" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6846344)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;">JamaisJ</a></span>, can you elaborate a bit here to better help the author?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>There's a lot of really cool things going on here,</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Can you be more specific about what you liked here, and why? As an aside, the majority of the community isn't too keen on the typical overused &quot;rage state&quot; powers approach (that sort of formulaic setup has often been seen in low-rated articles that wound up quickly deleted).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>but you need to pick a direction of some sort. There's no real narrative, just a lot of questions; solidify something in that regard.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What direction are you talking about here? Ongoing narrative involving the Foundation? Background context? Test logs with implications? What would you as a reader need to see solidified in order to be more interested in reading a draft of this material?</p>

